Data-section relocations for externally-defined symbols are emitted with
symbol index 0, so the linker resolves them to NULL. Confirmed with
`readelf -r`: a same-TU `staticFn` gets a proper symbol index, an extern one
gets 0. Not specific to function pointers - `int *p = &externVar;` fails the
same way, and `const` makes no difference.

The fix belongs in the ELF symbol table emission (src/elf.c); the relocation
record itself is created correctly by fillReference() in src/codegen_common.c.

This is the root cause of a self-hosted EduCC segfaulting on every
`-experimental` compile - see docs/ir-codegen-design.md section 10.
